!! cmavo: ta'e (TAhE)



!!! Proposed Definition

Habitually. Subjective time tense. Indicates that the event occurs habitually over a certain interval. When taggin a sumti, the sumti specifies the interval.



!!! Proposed Tag

fi'o jai ze'a tcaci



!!! See Also

* {di'i}

* {na'o}

* {ru'i}



!!! Proposed Keywords

* habitually

* habit

* out of habit



!!! Usage Examples

;.i .ai mi ba ta'e vreji minji lojbo bo bacru ca le nu cadzu:"I intend to habitually record my blatherings during my walks."

(This one was difficult to translate directly, so this is extremely glossed.)



!!! Notes





!!! Issues

The sense of "habit" is commonly ignored in usage in favor of a more general word indicating that the event is common/normal/ordinary. Otherwise it would make little sense to use it for events that don't involve an agent, e.g. {lo }. The difference between {ta'e}'s usage and the intended meaning of {na'o} is almost undistinguishable as things stand. Current usage has {ta'e} as {fi'o jai ze'a fadni} and {na'o} is almost never used.



